               not only allowed the taxonomic identification of past aquatic
               microbial communities but also enabled tracing their evolution
               and adaptation to episodic disturbances and gradual environmental
               change. Nevertheless, some challenges remain for scientists to
               take full advantage of the rapidly developing field of
               paleo-genetics, including the limited ability to detect rare taxa
