  volume    =  14,
  number    =  5,
  pages     = "e11337",
  abstract  = "Islands have been used as model systems to study ecological and
               evolutionary processes, and they provide an ideal set-up for
               validating new biodiversity monitoring methods. The application
               of environmental DNA metabarcoding for monitoring marine
               biodiversity requires an understanding of the spatial scale of
